Z||000000||KevinP||11-19-2000||05:27 PM||||I was re-evaluating my "wish" list for my car, and lowering springs were pretty high on the list.  So I got to thinking, my rear struts are pretty shot, and the front shocks are long overdue for replacement too.  Is there any method of lowering a car (springs or otherwise) that would be close to the cost of new shocks and struts?  I did some basic digging, I got a price of $70 each for struts, and $25 for shocks.  How much do springs go for?  $200 isn't much to play with, but I wanted to see what my options are as far as lowering is concerned.  Thanks,<P>Kevin<BR>'84 bumping 800 watts||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||11-19-2000||05:48 PM||||although its not back on the road, yet, i have done the following:<BR>monroe front shocks... $22 pair. advance auto<BR>gabriel rear struts... $65 pair. autozone<BR>Eibach springs........ $180 set. carparts<P>their is a coupon for 33% of at carparts.  do a search under general chat (past 30 days) for coupons.<P>of course i spent $700 (or more)on tie rod ends, steering rack, ball joints, bushings, and rear brakes!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">   <BR>We are not alone!||||reg||1
